WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.834
-Donald Trump was back
in a New York courtroom today

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.067
for the civil fraud trial

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.667
that could wipe out
his business empire,

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.634
less than a day
after his struggling rivals

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:11.801
for the GOP nomination gathered
for a mostly meaningless debate

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:13.467
in which they attacked
each other.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.467
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:19.434
♪♪

00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:21.901
Last night, the non-Trump
Republican candidates

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.701
gathered for yet
another pointless debate

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:25.667
on a little-watched network
called NewsNation,

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:28.000
where they all pretended
they were running for president,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.234
despite the fact
that they're roughly

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:31.000
50 points
behind the frontrunner.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.367
Watching these people
debate without Trump

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.400
is like watching
the Jets play each other.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.701
Now, in fairness,
I shouldn't be so glib.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.434
I may disagree
with these people,

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:40.868
but they've stepped up to take

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:42.400
on the responsibility
of leadership.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.734
And who knows,
maybe there's a chance

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:45.467
they'll beat Trump
and become the nominee.

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:48.467
So I do think we should at least
listen to what they have to say.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:51.334
-Welcome to the fourth
and final --

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:54.400
-Just kidding.
No one gives a [bleep].

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.100
Why should I --
Why should I act like any of

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.968
these people are actually
running against Donald Trump,

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.634
when they won't even act

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:03.934
like they're running
against Donald Trump?

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.934
They spent the whole debate
fighting with each other

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.501
like pigeons fighting
over a French fry

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:08.834
in the parking lot
of a restaurant

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:10.400
that is owned by
a much bigger pigeon.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.367
In case you missed it --
Sorry.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.701
Because you missed it,

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:17.667
here's a quick recap
of all these dweebs

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:19.100
taking shots at each other.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.567
-She will cave to the donors.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.033
She will not stand up for you.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:24.200
-He's mad because those
Wall Street donors

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.133
used to support him,
and now they support me.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.400
In terms of these donors

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.467
that are supporting me,
they're just jealous.

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.100
They wish that
they were supporting them.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.901
That is not true.
-I rejected them,

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.934
so I have a record of
standing up and do what's right.

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:36.868
And here's the thing.
-You have a record of lying.

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.167
-That's no reasonable --
-That's not my deal.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.000
-Yes,
it's exactly what you said.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.834
-[ Indistinct ]
-You do this at every debate.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.934
You say -- No, no,
don't interrupt me.

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:45.701
I didn't interrupt you.
-Hold on.

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:48.234
-Excuse me, Chris, I'm speaking
and I'm not done yet.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:50.567
You had your chance,
and we're going to be done.

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:52.334
I think that that's
what people need to know.

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.367
Nikki is corrupt.

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.200
-This is the fourth debate --

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.601
the fourth debate that you would
be voted in the first 20 minutes

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:02.033
as the most obnoxious blowhard
in America.

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:04.033
-Hey, hey, everyone!
Break it up.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:07.033
There's no need to fight!
You're all obnoxious blowhards.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:08.534
And yet, based on the polls,
your problem

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:09.934
is you don't blow hard enough.

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:12.767
Although, I will say,
if there's one service

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:14.734
anyone could perform
at these stupid debates,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.767
it's tearing Vivek Ramaswamy
to shreds.

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:18.467
I mean, allow me
to borrow the parlance

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.167
of my outer borough brethren,
when I say

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:23.434
this [bleep] guy!

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:26.400
Now, if you somehow managed
to find NewsNation on your TV

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.534
guide somewhere up there between
the pay-per-view curling channel

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:31.968
and those channels
that are just music...

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:34.934
Who are those for?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.868
Can we do a "Closer Look"
on that one day?

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.300
"Hey, you want to hear
some tunes?

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.934
I'll put it on channel 985
on the TV.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:43.133
I have it in HD."

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:45.534
Why does that matter?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:46.934
Anyway,

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:48.767
if you actually tuned
into the second-place debate,

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.167
you were probably frustrated
by the fact

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:52.868
that none of the candidates,
except for Christie,

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:54.100
bothered to go after Trump
at all,

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.868
who is leading them
by a huge margin.

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:58.167
At one point,
both the moderators and Christie

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:01.334
repeatedly gave Florida Governor
Ron DeSantis a clear opening

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:04.634
to say the obvious, that Trump
is unfit to serve as president,

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.634
and DeSantis
wouldn't even say that.

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:08.300
-You seem to be saying
Donald Trump

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.534
is no longer mentally fit
to be president.

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:11.901
Is that what you think?

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:15.234
-Look, he is showing
Father Time is undefeated.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.367
He got the nomination.
-But do you think

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:17.634
he's mentally fit
to be president?

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:19.501
-I think we need to have
somebody younger.

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:21.434
-Why doesn't he just answer
the question?

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.133
The question was very direct.

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:26.734
Is he fit to be president
or isn't he?

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:28.467
Is he fit or isn't he?
-We do not want to do --

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.434
You're talking about him being
80 years old.

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:32.701
Ron, is he fit?
-[ Indistinct ]

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:35.133
-Governor, DeSantis --
-Ron, Ron, Ron, Ron,

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:36.968
is he fit or isn't he?

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:38.834
-[ Indistinct ]
-So, you do think he's fit?

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:40.100
You do think?
-You should not

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.501
nominate somebody...
-He won't answer.

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:43.934
-...who's almost 80 years old.

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:46.501
-He's afraid to answer.
-No, I'm not.

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:49.434
-My God, how hard is it
to say Donald Trump is unfit?

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:51.334
He's mentally unfit.
He's physically unfit.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:55.267
He's politically unfit.
Even his clothes are unfit.

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:58.267
He's facing four indictments,
fomented a violent coup attempt,

00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:00.634
forgets which city he's in,
who he's running against,

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:01.901
thinks windmills cause cancer,

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:03.767
and once said
there were airports

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.200
during the Revolutionary War,

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.767
because everyone remembers
that famous painting

00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:12.200
of George Washington
taxiing across the runway.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.634
Although, in fairness, if you've
ever flown out of LaGuardia,

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:17.067
you'd think it was built
in the 1700s, too.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:18.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:19.868
You know what's a bummer?

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:22.567
Joke isn't true anymore,

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:24.067
'cause they redid LaGuardia

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:25.501
and it's so nice now.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:30.300
It's so -- It's the only
New York airport I use anymore,

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.000
and I don't even use it
as an airport.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.167
Once a week my wife
and I go for date night.

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:37.968
We have a nice meal,

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:39.801
let TSA get a little frisky
with us,

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:40.667
then we just go home.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:43.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.701
[bleep] love LaGuardia.

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:46.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:50.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:53.167
It's no kind of life.

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:54.334
Anyway, where was I?

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:56.133
Oh, right.
Christie and DeSantis.

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:57.567
Watching these two argue
with each other

00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.400
is like watching Master Shake

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.868
yell at Meatwad on
"Aqua Teen Hunger Force."

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.000
And if you're
wondering who's who,

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.901
allow me to remind you
that Donald Trump

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:07.334
is the one who coined the term
"Meatball Ron,"

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:09.501
a nickname so perfect it stuck

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:11.734
even though Trump
doesn't actually use it.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.100
You almost feel for DeSantis.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.334
He thought this was his time --
darling of the right,

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:17.067
governor of the third
most populous state,

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:19.000
built a huge reserve
of campaign donations.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.467
And then one day an adviser
comes in and says, "Bad news.

00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:22.968
Trump called you Meatball Ron."

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:25.234
And DeSantis said, "So what?
It's not going to stick, is it?"

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:26.267
Turned to his wife, said,

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:27.701
"Do you think it'll stick,
Casey?"

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:29.234
And she said, "I don't think you
have anything to worry about,

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:31.701
Meatball Ron -- I mean Ron!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:33.367
I'm gonna take the kids home.

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:37.067
Say bye to Meatball Dad --
I mean Dad!"

00:05:37.067 --> 00:05:39.400
So no one in the GOP actually
wants to take

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.634
on the front runner,
despite his obvious weaknesses.

00:05:41.634 --> 00:05:43.133
Just this morning,
he was back in court

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:45.067
for the $250 million
civil fraud trial

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:48.200
that could decimate his business
empire and his personal fortune.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.934
He was once again
sitting at the defense table,

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:52.901
scowling in front of a computer
screen like a teen at the DMV,

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:56.868
forced to watch a video about
the dangers of drunk driving.

00:05:56.868 --> 00:05:59.234
Before entering the courtroom,
he did his usual shtick where

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:01.300
he called the trial a witch hunt
and all that nonsense.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:04.000
But he also claimed today's
testimony would vindicate him

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.434
and that the banks actually
think he's innocent as well.

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:08.834
-So we're going in now.
We have an expert witness,

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:12.400
one of the great experts
in the country.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.100
And I hope you'll all be able
to listen to him.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.834
But it'll just be another day.

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:22.934
If you look at -- If you look at
the case, we did nothing wrong.

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:25.567
There were no victims.
The bank loves us.

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:28.567
The bank testified.
They love us.

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:31.334
We did absolutely nothing wrong.
We never even defaulted.

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:34.300
We never had a default letter
sent to us.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.300
The bank said we were
a perfect customer.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.501
-In what context would a bank

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:39.167
even call you a perfect
customer?

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:40.868
[ As Trump ] "You know,
I was at the bank once

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:45.467
and an ATM came up to me --
big ATM, strong ATM --

00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:48.601
tears pouring down its screen
onto its disgusting keypad,

00:06:48.601 --> 00:06:49.901
and it said to me,
it said, 'Sir,

00:06:49.901 --> 00:06:51.067
you're a perfect customer.'

00:06:51.067 --> 00:06:54.067
And I said, I said,
'Thank you, ATM machine,'

00:06:54.067 --> 00:06:56.033
and it said,
'The M stands for machine.

00:06:56.033 --> 00:06:57.701
You don't need to say it twice.'

00:06:57.701 --> 00:07:00.400
And I said, 'You're wrong.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.400
The M stands for Meatball Ron.'"

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.167
Trump's court appearance comes
two days after he once again

00:07:09.167 --> 00:07:11.534
sent shockwaves of anxiety
throughout the political world

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:13.367
by claiming he would be
a dictator

00:07:13.367 --> 00:07:16.501
if he wins a second time,
but only on day one.

00:07:16.501 --> 00:07:18.701
That answer came in response
to persistent questioning

00:07:18.701 --> 00:07:21.334
by Fox host Sean Hannity,
who was trying to get Trump

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:23.267
to refute reports
that he and his allies

00:07:23.267 --> 00:07:25.400
are drawing up plans to use
the Justice Department

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:26.868
to get revenge on his critics.

00:07:26.868 --> 00:07:29.667
But Trump refused
to follow Hannity's lead.

00:07:29.667 --> 00:07:34.400
-To be clear, do you in any way
have any plans whatsoever

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:38.267
if reelected president
to abuse power,

00:07:38.267 --> 00:07:42.167
to break the law, to use the
government to go after people?

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:44.100
-You mean like
they're using right now?

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:47.934
-Under no circumstances you are
promising America tonight

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:51.534
you would never abuse power
as retribution

00:07:51.534 --> 00:07:54.501
against anybody.
-Except for day one.

00:07:54.501 --> 00:07:55.767
-Except for --
-Look. He's going crazy.

00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:57.501
Except for day one.
-Meaning?

00:07:57.501 --> 00:08:01.901
-I want to close the border and
I want to drill, drill, drill.

00:08:01.901 --> 00:08:04.467
-That's not retribution.

00:08:04.467 --> 00:08:05.801
I got it.
-I'm going to be --

00:08:05.801 --> 00:08:08.067
I'm going to be --
You know, he keeps...

00:08:08.067 --> 00:08:09.801
I love this guy.

00:08:09.801 --> 00:08:11.701
He says, "You're not going
to be a dictator, are you?"

00:08:11.701 --> 00:08:14.167
I said, "No, no, no.
Other than day one."

00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:15.634
-I will say, I love
how much Trump

00:08:15.634 --> 00:08:17.033
enjoys making Hannity miserable.

00:08:17.033 --> 00:08:18.968
Hannity was clearly trying
to help Trump out,

00:08:18.968 --> 00:08:20.234
and Trump laughed in his face

00:08:20.234 --> 00:08:21.834
like he was Joe Pesci
about to whack him.

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:23.901
[ As Pesci ] "This guy! I love
this guy! He's a funny guy.

00:08:23.901 --> 00:08:25.701
Hey, let's take a ride
out to the woods together.

00:08:25.701 --> 00:08:27.567
Get in my car."

00:08:27.567 --> 00:08:29.000
Whenever Hannity
interviews Trump,

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.033
there's this weird dynamic
where Hannity, the interviewer,

00:08:31.033 --> 00:08:33.067
is desperately
trying not to make news,

00:08:33.067 --> 00:08:34.567
and Trump, the candidate,
is like,

00:08:34.567 --> 00:08:35.601
"Sean,
this is boring as [bleep].

00:08:35.601 --> 00:08:36.701
I'm going to make some news."

00:08:36.701 --> 00:08:38.901
And now Trump's allies are mad,

00:08:38.901 --> 00:08:40.267
not that Trump said
he'd be a dictator,

00:08:40.267 --> 00:08:42.734
but that Hannity asked him
the question in the first place.

00:08:42.734 --> 00:08:45.000
Here's Trump's ally and
fellow criminals, Steve Bannon,

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.767
who was himself charged with
fraud before Trump pardoned him

00:08:47.767 --> 00:08:50.534
and has been convicted
of contempt of Congress charges,

00:08:50.534 --> 00:08:52.868
tearing into Hannity
on his weird Internet show.

00:08:52.868 --> 00:08:55.200
-Sean Hannity actually thought
he was helping Trump last night.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.267
Let me ask you the question.
Will you be a dictator?

00:08:57.267 --> 00:08:59.934
Trump gives a full heckle.

00:08:59.934 --> 00:09:02.367
And here's what I love.
The audience gets it.

00:09:02.367 --> 00:09:04.400
They're laughing.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.200
By the way, Sean,
they're laughing at you.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.334
They're laughing at the stupid,
ridiculous question.

00:09:09.334 --> 00:09:10.634
Of course,
Trump's not a dictator.

00:09:10.634 --> 00:09:13.634
It's absurd on the face
of even to consider.

00:09:13.634 --> 00:09:15.234
Even to ask that question
that "Morning Joe"

00:09:15.234 --> 00:09:17.400
and those guys can cut
the clips on shows

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.267
you're an idiot.

00:09:19.267 --> 00:09:22.501
And we don't
have time for idiots, bro.

00:09:22.501 --> 00:09:26.100
This is a -- This is a war.
How dumb are you?

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:29.467
We're playing for keeps.
This is war.

00:09:29.467 --> 00:09:30.767
And you're just not good enough

00:09:30.767 --> 00:09:32.367
and you're just not
smart enough.

00:09:32.367 --> 00:09:34.534
-I love how Bannon
can both say it's crazy

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:35.868
to use words like dictator

00:09:35.868 --> 00:09:41.901
while also hammering home,
"We're at war...bro."

00:09:41.901 --> 00:09:44.100
And I do believe Bannon
thinks we're in a war

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:46.300
because he always looks like
he's been living in a bunker

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:49.367
or, I don't know,
the inside of a dryer.

00:09:49.367 --> 00:09:50.667
I love watching
all these horrible people

00:09:50.667 --> 00:09:51.534
fight with each other.

00:09:51.534 --> 00:09:53.100
Christie calling
Vivek obnoxious,

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.467
Trump calling DeSantis
a meatball,

00:09:54.467 --> 00:09:55.834
Bannon calling Hannity idiot.

00:09:55.834 --> 00:09:57.534
Nobody calling Trump
anything lest he eat them

00:09:57.534 --> 00:09:58.834
like a French fry.

00:09:58.834 --> 00:10:01.767
It's such a striking contrast
with the other side.

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:03.133
Say what you will
about Democrats,

00:10:03.133 --> 00:10:04.501
but there was never any
name calling at their debates.

00:10:04.501 --> 00:10:06.133
The most aggressive thing
that ever happened

00:10:06.133 --> 00:10:08.767
at a Democratic debate
was Bernie shooting his hand up

00:10:08.767 --> 00:10:10.434
in the air
to answer a question like

00:10:10.434 --> 00:10:13.534
he was trying to hail
a cab in a rainstorm.

00:10:13.534 --> 00:10:16.033
[ As Sanders ]
"99% of the taxis

00:10:16.033 --> 00:10:19.334
have a go at
the 1% of the passengers!"

00:10:19.334 --> 00:10:21.000
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.567
The far and away
GOP front runner

00:10:22.567 --> 00:10:24.701
confessed he'll be a dictator,
was in court today for a fraud

00:10:24.701 --> 00:10:26.467
trial, and faces
four more criminal indictments.

00:10:26.467 --> 00:10:28.934
And yet none of his GOP rivals
want to take him on.

00:10:28.934 --> 00:10:30.701
I would spend more time
recapping the debate,

00:10:30.701 --> 00:10:32.534
but this show is only
an hour long and...

00:10:32.534 --> 00:10:34.934
-We don't have
time for idiots, bro.

00:10:34.934 --> 00:10:36.434
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:36.434 --> 00:10:40.400
♪♪

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:42.868
Hey, a quick message
for our Canadian viewers.

00:10:42.868 --> 00:10:44.267
This is very exciting news.

00:10:44.267 --> 00:10:47.100
Our videos were not available on
YouTube for the last few months.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.968
They are now back on YouTube,

00:10:48.968 --> 00:10:51.133
and we also want
to say thanks to CTV

00:10:51.133 --> 00:10:54.567
who is airing our shows in
their entirety on their network.

00:10:54.567 --> 00:10:55.968
Check them out there as well.

00:10:55.968 --> 00:10:58.234
Thank you, Canada.

00:10:58.234 --> 00:10:59.300
Good luck with everything.

